00:22:15.700 --> 00:22:17.700
You know, with your competitive streak,

00:22:17.700 --> 00:22:19.700
I'm surprised you forfeited this one to Lois.

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:21.700
Huh! Competition, Lois?

00:22:21.700 --> 00:22:24.700
I'm shocking this one up to pro bono.

00:22:24.700 --> 00:22:25.700
Yeah, right.

00:22:25.700 --> 00:22:27.700
Okay, so idle hands aren't really my thing.

00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:28.700
I got the safe time.

00:22:28.700 --> 00:22:30.700
report on the arrows.

00:22:30.700 --> 00:22:34.700
They're made from an advanced titanium alloy that is untraceable.

00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:35.700
What about the ring?

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:39.700
None of the shots I scanned on my computer came out to have a clean image.

00:22:39.700 --> 00:22:45.700
However, I may have forgotten to mention to Lois that my computer is compiling them to render a new one.

00:22:45.700 --> 00:22:57.299
Look, you can tell the mail room to stop forwarding these bogus claims.

00:22:57.299 --> 00:23:02.299
Well, I highly doubt the green arrow is going to out himself on a Hello Kitty notepad.

00:23:02.299 --> 00:23:36.579
Clerk, she's in trouble.

00:23:36.579 --> 00:23:45.549
Lewis?

00:23:45.549 --> 00:23:48.599
Looks like someone took her.

00:23:48.599 --> 00:23:54.369
Took her.

00:23:54.369 --> 00:23:55.369
What are you talking about?

00:23:55.369 --> 00:23:56.369
Who would do that?

00:23:56.369 --> 00:23:57.369
Isn't it obvious?

00:23:57.369 --> 00:23:58.369
The Green Arrow.

00:23:58.369 --> 00:24:02.839
What makes you think he'd have anything to do with this?

00:24:02.839 --> 00:24:06.839
He's wanted all over town for armed robbery.

00:24:06.839 --> 00:24:10.839
Lois is the one who publicly threatened unmasked the guy.

00:24:10.839 --> 00:24:12.839
Guess he doesn't live by a coat of honor.

00:24:12.839 --> 00:24:18.900
Because it's not the same as yours?

00:24:18.900 --> 00:24:22.900
Maybe if you were as interested in finding out about this guy as you weren't catching him,

00:24:22.900 --> 00:24:28.380
you would have realized that everything he's stolen so far has been bought off the black market.

00:24:28.380 --> 00:24:29.380
You're seeing Lionel's necklace?

00:24:29.380 --> 00:24:30.380
Yeah.

00:24:30.380 --> 00:24:32.380
It's exactly what I'm saying.

00:24:32.380 --> 00:24:35.380
You've been on this hunt to return it to its original thief?

00:24:35.380 --> 00:24:40.539
You think Lionel took her?

00:24:40.539 --> 00:25:09.220
I think there are a lot of people out there that would go to any length to catch the green arrow.

00:25:09.220 --> 00:25:11.220
Chloe, it's too late. There's no sign of her.

00:25:11.220 --> 00:25:13.220
Well, I might have something that'll help.

00:25:13.220 --> 00:25:20.000
The image from the ring finally rendered, and I'm sending it to you right now.

00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:21.000
It's a family crest.

00:25:21.000 --> 00:25:24.000
The only problem is ye old crests makers weren't very creative.

00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:27.000
I mean, there's thousands of them and they're all practically identical.

00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:29.000
It's going to take me a little while to track this one down.

00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:33.400
I've seen this before.

00:25:33.400 --> 00:25:34.400
Clark?

00:25:34.400 --> 00:25:37.000
Hello?

00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:39.569
Hello?

00:25:39.569 --> 00:28:02.500
Wouldn't have the stones to face.

00:28:02.500 --> 00:28:05.500
And like you don't know, that Errol Flynn wannabe put you guys up to this.

00:28:05.500 --> 00:28:21.500
Has made a joke of the firm I've worked my life to build.

00:28:21.500 --> 00:28:25.500
It's walked off with more than 30 million from my clients.

00:28:25.500 --> 00:28:28.500
Then why am I the one with bruises on my knees right now?

00:28:28.500 --> 00:28:34.500
Because you splashed my humiliation across the front page of the paper.

00:28:34.500 --> 00:28:36.500
And now you're going to help me rectify that.

00:28:36.500 --> 00:28:38.500
Let me rectify that.

00:28:38.500 --> 00:28:58.769
I don't know who he is.

00:28:58.769 --> 00:28:59.769
She doesn't know anything.

00:28:59.769 --> 00:30:34.059
I know black male was one of your talents.

00:30:34.059 --> 00:30:38.059
Lex, um, I know I went behind your back, but I wanted to do this my way.

00:30:38.059 --> 00:30:40.059
And if you're mad...

00:30:40.059 --> 00:30:50.609
Actually, I'm impressed.

00:30:50.609 --> 00:30:59.250
I've never had anyone try to protect me like that.

00:30:59.250 --> 00:31:01.250
Lex, we have a serious problem.

00:31:01.250 --> 00:31:03.250
Your father.

00:31:03.250 --> 00:31:09.490
He isn't going to stop until he gets that black box away from you.

00:31:09.490 --> 00:31:11.490
Because he's afraid of what I'll do.

00:31:11.490 --> 00:31:15.440
What about you?

00:31:15.440 --> 00:31:18.440
Is there a party that wonders the same thing?

00:31:18.440 --> 00:31:21.170
No.

00:31:21.170 --> 00:31:27.869
I believe in you.

00:31:27.869 --> 00:31:32.869
But Lex, there is something that I haven't been completely honest with you about.

00:31:32.869 --> 00:31:48.599
I knew the box was a weapon.

00:31:48.599 --> 00:31:51.599
If the box is that dangerous,

00:31:51.599 --> 00:32:00.619
you want me to shut the project down, don't you?

00:32:00.619 --> 00:32:03.619
Lex, it might be the only thing that will save us from them next time.

00:32:03.619 --> 00:32:43.180
Are you okay?

00:32:43.180 --> 00:32:46.180
No thanks to you.

00:32:46.180 --> 00:32:51.920
I see.

00:32:51.920 --> 00:32:52.920
saved you.

00:32:52.920 --> 00:32:53.920
Yeah.

00:32:53.920 --> 00:32:55.920
From goons who are trying to find you.

00:32:55.920 --> 00:32:59.920
They're not the only one with a V for vendetta on your little leather ass.

00:32:59.920 --> 00:33:00.920
Little.

00:33:00.920 --> 00:33:02.920
I really been working the glutes lately, too.

00:33:02.920 --> 00:33:04.920
Did the humor come with a costume?

00:33:04.920 --> 00:33:08.920
Did the Tomb Raider routine come from wanting Daddy's attention?

00:33:08.920 --> 00:33:16.880
Oops. Guess my aim's a little rusty.

00:33:16.880 --> 00:33:24.640
Now, let's take off those glasses and unveil our Prince of Thieves, shall we?

00:33:24.640 --> 00:33:56.940
Oliver Queen.

00:33:56.940 --> 00:33:57.940
You owe me one.

00:33:57.940 --> 00:34:10.670
That was you on the roof? Why'd you let me get away?

00:34:10.670 --> 00:34:17.420
I'm not sure Lois would understand why her new boyfriend leads a double life.

00:34:17.420 --> 00:34:27.079
Or why one of her best friends does the same thing?

00:34:27.079 --> 00:34:29.079
I think we're even.

00:34:29.079 --> 00:34:31.079
It'll be even when you returned that you stole from Lionel.

00:34:31.079 --> 00:34:54.650
Chloe, what's all the buzz?

00:34:54.650 --> 00:34:59.650
Seven stolen artifacts were anonymously returned to the Met, the Tate, and the Louvre.

00:34:59.650 --> 00:35:02.650
Looks like you've got some friendly competition in the Night and Shining Armour Arena.

00:35:02.650 --> 00:35:05.650
The guy has a couple good things and he goes from villain to hero overnight.

00:35:05.650 --> 00:35:08.650
Clark, every time he strikes some corrupt,

00:35:08.650 --> 00:35:10.650
Tycoon, an anonymous donation to some charity,

00:35:10.650 --> 00:35:12.650
mysteriously appears the next day.

00:35:12.650 --> 00:35:14.650
And you don't care how many laws are broken to get it there?

00:35:14.650 --> 00:35:16.650
Oh, I guess that's just the price of justice.

00:35:16.650 --> 00:35:18.650
I mean, if you ask me, he's a modern-day Robin Hood.

00:35:18.650 --> 00:35:21.650
That still doesn't mean I'm not dying to find out who he is, though.

00:35:21.650 --> 00:35:25.650
Oh, hey, I never heard back from you after I sent you the picture of that crest.

00:35:25.650 --> 00:35:27.650
I kind of ran into a dead end.

00:35:27.650 --> 00:35:34.739
It's funny, so did I.

00:35:34.739 --> 00:35:39.739
All my files on the ring are gone, including the backup files, Clark.

00:35:39.739 --> 00:35:43.599
Just don't look into them, Chloe.

00:35:43.599 --> 00:35:48.980
You know.

00:35:48.980 --> 00:35:50.980
who he is, don't you?

00:35:50.980 --> 00:35:57.119
It's a favor to me. Please don't.

00:35:57.119 --> 00:35:59.119
And he knows who you are.

00:35:59.119 --> 00:36:04.119
Well, I guess there's some sort of secret code of honor among superheroes.

00:36:04.119 --> 00:36:17.699
What do we have here?

00:36:17.699 --> 00:36:19.699
Yeah, not bad for a rookie, huh?

00:36:19.699 --> 00:36:23.699
It's really incredible. You know, you have every newspaper in the country calling this guy the Green Arrow.

00:36:23.699 --> 00:36:25.699
It's got a real following.

00:36:25.699 --> 00:36:32.699
Yeah, well, so did Charles Manson.

00:36:32.699 --> 00:36:36.699
I know this is a rare moment for you, but, um, you know, maybe you're overreacting.

00:36:36.699 --> 00:36:37.699
It's not like you.

00:36:37.699 --> 00:36:38.699
This guy's a killer.

00:36:38.699 --> 00:36:41.699
Ollie, he's a threat to Metropolis.

00:36:41.699 --> 00:36:44.699
And I'm not going to stop until I find out who he is.

00:36:44.699 --> 00:36:45.699
Trust me.

00:36:45.699 --> 00:36:47.699
You don't know the Green Arrow like I do.

00:36:47.699 --> 00:37:13.150
Not that I'd ever question your theatrical skills.

00:37:13.150 --> 00:37:15.150
But you really had Lana convinced.

00:37:15.150 --> 00:37:18.719
Thank you, Dad.

00:37:18.719 --> 00:37:22.719
Just following the script, the script that you gave me, son.

00:37:22.719 --> 00:37:30.409
But, you know, if you really want to have an honest relationship with Lana,

00:37:30.409 --> 00:37:31.409
you should stop testing her.

00:37:31.409 --> 00:37:37.650
Well, I had to be sure.

00:37:37.650 --> 00:37:40.650
Another important lesson you taught me.

00:37:40.650 --> 00:37:45.650
The greater the trust, the greater the betrayal.

00:37:45.650 --> 00:37:50.840
Thanks.

00:37:50.840 --> 00:37:56.179
What do I have to do to prove to you that I want to be a part of your life?

00:37:56.179 --> 00:37:59.179
Part of my life or part of the project?

00:37:59.179 --> 00:38:04.179
I would never have told you about the box if you hadn't already known.

00:38:04.179 --> 00:38:09.329
But that's as close as you're ever going to get to it.

00:38:09.329 --> 00:38:23.780
So what makes you think that I won't tell Lana Lang about the obstacle course you set up for her if I'm so untrustworthy?

00:38:23.780 --> 00:38:33.500
Because you've put so much effort into fooling the Kent's that you're a good man.

00:38:33.500 --> 00:38:36.500
You're starting to believe it yourself.

00:38:36.500 --> 00:39:01.539
I didn't realize that was such a fascinating subject.

00:39:01.539 --> 00:39:05.429
You've been reading up on me.

00:39:05.429 --> 00:39:07.429
You and Lois ought to start a fan club.

00:39:07.429 --> 00:39:14.230
You're going to tell her?

00:39:14.230 --> 00:39:18.230
I don't know, Clark. You know, you seem to be doing a pretty good job skating by with this farm boy charade.

00:39:18.230 --> 00:39:20.230
Arm-boy charade.

00:39:20.230 --> 00:39:24.230
You can't be with someone unless I know who you really are.

00:39:24.230 --> 00:39:26.230
Trust me, I've tried.

00:39:26.230 --> 00:39:28.230
You lost her, Lex.

00:39:28.230 --> 00:39:33.909
Is that why you hate me, Clark?

00:39:33.909 --> 00:39:37.909
Because I'm just another silver spoon-fed rich boy, is that it?

00:39:37.909 --> 00:39:43.059
Or is it because I'm not willing to play the martyr like you?

00:39:43.059 --> 00:39:46.059
You can play this game as long as you want.

00:39:46.059 --> 00:39:48.059
But sooner or later, you can hurt her.

00:39:48.059 --> 00:39:52.530
You know that.

00:39:52.530 --> 00:39:54.530
Well, you seem to have all the answers.

00:39:54.530 --> 00:39:58.030
So I guess it's a good thing I've decided to put this into safer hands.

00:39:58.030 --> 00:40:08.719
With a record, Lionel bought that off a notorious Bosnian warlord.

00:40:08.719 --> 00:40:11.219
Used it to launder Luther Court money.

00:40:11.219 --> 00:40:12.719
So why give it to me?

00:40:12.719 --> 00:40:20.429
Well, you seem to have a crystal clear idea of what's right and what's wrong.

00:40:20.429 --> 00:40:22.429
You decide who it belongs to.

00:40:22.429 --> 00:40:30.639
It's not as clear as it used to be.

00:40:30.639 --> 00:40:33.639
You really think it's right to steal as long as it goes to a good cause.

00:40:33.639 --> 00:40:36.639
At the end justifies the means?

00:40:36.639 --> 00:40:39.639
Absolutely yes.

00:40:39.639 --> 00:40:42.360
I'll never feel that way.

00:40:42.360 --> 00:40:51.469
You said you didn't know me one.

00:40:51.469 --> 00:40:53.469
It's why you really here.

00:40:53.469 --> 00:40:57.579
Clark, you have abilities.

00:40:57.579 --> 00:40:59.579
I couldn't even dream of.

00:40:59.579 --> 00:41:04.789
And I admire that you use them to save the people you're close to.

00:41:04.789 --> 00:41:11.159
But there's a whole world of people out there, Clark.

00:41:11.159 --> 00:41:13.159
They need us.

00:41:13.159 --> 00:41:22.239
With your potential, you can't wait for him to come to you.

00:41:22.239 --> 00:41:32.860
And you're ready to do something about that.

00:41:32.860 --> 00:41:33.860
You let me know.

00:41:33.860 --> 00:41:34.860
You let me know.

